00:13:09,581 --> 00:13:14,878
He said I was intimidated by his intelligence, and then, he offered to be my "leader."

258
00:14:00,716 --> 00:14:02,009
Do you know this sonata?

259
00:14:02,259 --> 00:14:03,259
No.

260
00:14:03,719 --> 00:14:05,178
How long have you played the piano?

261
00:14:06,471 --> 00:14:07,931
I don't play piano.

262
00:14:09,766 --> 00:14:11,724
George, you got any thoughts here?

263
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:13,352
I certainly do.

264
00:14:15,397 --> 00:14:16,397
Mary, tell him.

265
00:14:17,149 --> 00:14:19,192
It's simple. We don't have a choice.

266
00:14:19,401 --> 00:14:20,944
Well, you gave it a shot.

267
00:14:21,194 --> 00:14:22,834
We wish you luck with Sheldon elsewhere...

268
00:14:22,863 --> 00:14:24,781
No, no, no.

269
00:14:24,990 --> 00:14:25,990
We don't have a choice.

270
00:14:26,116 --> 00:14:27,116
He's got to stay here.

271
00:14:27,617 --> 00:14:29,077
We can't afford private school.

272
00:14:29,286 --> 00:14:30,454
I sure can't homeschool him.

273
00:14:30,662 --> 00:14:32,873
He's doing calculus and euclidean something or other.

274
00:14:33,081 --> 00:14:34,291
Euclidean geometry.

275
00:14:34,499 --> 00:14:35,876
Guess where I learned that.

276
00:14:36,084 --> 00:14:37,419
Yeah, yeah, we know.

277
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:44,319
All I care about is that my son gets the education he deserves, so you all are gonna have to figure this out.

278
00:14:44,343 --> 00:14:46,219
Coach, can you help me out here, please?

279
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:47,428
'Cause I'm dyin'.

280
00:14:51,350 --> 00:14:52,768
I'd rather not.

281
00:14:57,314 --> 00:14:58,565
G minor.

282
00:15:02,736 --> 00:15:03,736
E flat.

283
00:15:05,864 --> 00:15:06,864
C minor.

284
00:15:09,993 --> 00:15:11,411
You have perfect pitch.

285
00:15:11,787 --> 00:15:12,787
Okay.

286
00:15:13,497 --> 00:15:16,375
Sweetheart, you should really pursue music.

287
00:15:16,792 --> 00:15:19,169
No, thank you. Musicians take drugs.

288
00:15:20,462 --> 00:15:22,839
Is there a faculty restroom I could use?

289
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:28,552
♪ ooh...

290
00:15:29,930 --> 00:15:31,515
♪ ooh...

291
00:15:37,687 --> 00:15:38,855
Cooper, Stinson, you're up.

292
00:15:39,314 --> 00:15:42,150
Hey, look, it's the dumb brother.

293
00:15:44,736 --> 00:15:46,822
Okay.

294
00:15:52,494 --> 00:15:54,079
That's enough. Hey.

295
00:15:56,456 --> 00:15:57,616
Hey, that's enough!

296
00:15:57,666 --> 00:15:58,851
George sr.: Hey, hey! That's enough!

297
00:15:58,875 --> 00:15:59,875
Georgie.

298
00:16:00,377 --> 00:16:01,586
Georgie! Georgie!

299
00:16:01,795 --> 00:16:03,255
Stop! Stop!

300
00:16:06,174 --> 00:16:07,454
What the hell is wrong with you?

301
00:16:12,013 --> 00:16:13,013
You okay?

302
00:16:13,181 --> 00:16:15,142
No, I'm not okay.

303
00:16:24,151 --> 00:16:25,360
Where you think you're going?

304
00:16:25,569 --> 00:16:27,362
I quit. I don't want to play anymore!

305
00:16:27,571 --> 00:16:29,739
Since when? Since right now!

306
00:16:30,907 --> 00:16:32,033
All right, what is going on?

307
00:16:32,242 --> 00:16:34,202
What do you think's going on?!

308
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:36,580
You mean Sheldon?

309
00:16:39,541 --> 00:16:40,792
You can't let that bother you.

310
00:16:41,001 --> 00:16:42,127
It doesn't bother you?

311
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:43,935
You got called to the principal's office.

312
00:16:44,546 --> 00:16:46,381
Yeah, that wasn't so great.

313
00:16:46,590 --> 00:16:48,030
I can't be in the same school as him!

314
00:16:48,175 --> 00:16:49,695
Well, I don't see what choice you have.

315
00:16:49,801 --> 00:16:53,555
Right. Ever since he could talk, I quit having any choices.

316
00:17:00,729 --> 00:17:02,314
I know it's hard.

317
00:17:03,648 --> 00:17:08,851
I'm telling you, as your coach, quit your whining, get your uniform on and you get your ass back out there.

318
00:17:10,071 --> 00:17:11,573
But what about as my dad?

319
00:17:12,657 --> 00:17:14,367
Your dad is having a bad day.

320
00:17:14,576 --> 00:17:16,161
Listen to your coach.

321
00:17:22,042 --> 00:17:26,087
Can a clock be powered by an ordinary potato?

322
00:17:26,630 --> 00:17:31,843
I hope so, boys and girls, or this is going to be a really boring episode.

323
00:17:32,302 --> 00:17:33,386
The supplies you'll need...

324
00:17:33,595 --> 00:17:35,305
Why can't we watch ducktales?

325
00:17:35,514 --> 00:17:38,558
'Cause we don't learn anything watching ducktales.

326
00:17:38,934 --> 00:17:41,686
It's TV; We aren't supposed to learn.

327
00:17:41,895 --> 00:17:44,814
Two alligator grips and, let's see...

328
00:17:45,273 --> 00:17:47,108
Of course, a clock.

329
00:17:47,317 --> 00:17:49,557
Missy, go somewhere else. I need to talk to your brother.

330
00:17:49,903 --> 00:17:52,280
Why don't you go somewhere else and I can watch duck...

331
00:17:52,489 --> 00:17:53,489
Go!

332
00:17:54,199 --> 00:17:55,367
I hate everybody.

333
00:17:55,825 --> 00:17:58,328
It's time for science.

334
00:18:01,331 --> 00:18:04,334
Hey, he was about to power a clock with a potato.

335
00:18:04,543 --> 00:18:05,293
Not possible.

336
00:18:05,502 --> 00:18:07,379
Now, listen... Am I in trouble?

337
00:18:07,921 --> 00:18:08,921
No.

338
00:18:09,798 --> 00:18:11,258
Maybe. Just listen.

339
00:18:13,635 --> 00:18:16,972
You're not gonna make it in this school if you keep ratting people out.

340
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:20,100
But they were breaking the grooming codes and the dress codes.

341
00:18:20,308 --> 00:18:23,270
I saw one boy with a t-shirt that said...

342
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:24,896
"Bite me."

343
00:18:25,105 --> 00:18:27,315
Yeah. That-that's terrible.

344
00:18:28,149 --> 00:18:29,734
Sheldon, let me tell you a little story.

345
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:32,263
Did you ever wonder why we moved from galveston to medford?

346
00:18:32,696 --> 00:18:35,782
No. I tend to wonder about the bigger questions.

347
00:18:35,991 --> 00:18:37,784
Okay, well, here's why.

348
00:18:38,451 --> 00:18:43,415
Your dad had a real good coaching job and I saw some grown-ups breaking rules.

349
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:44,499
What'd they do?

350
00:18:44,708 --> 00:18:46,376
I-It's kind of complicated, but...

351
00:18:47,252 --> 00:18:51,214
Football coaches aren't allowed to recruit kids from other high schools to play on their teams.

352
00:18:51,423 --> 00:18:52,549
And you told on them?

353
00:18:52,757 --> 00:18:54,759
Yeah. You know what happened?

354
00:18:54,968 --> 00:18:57,596
Justice descended upon the rule breakers?

355
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,473
I got fired, Sheldon.

356
00:19:01,266 --> 00:19:02,976
And I got a bad reputation.

357
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:06,813
Oh. That's why you drink so much beer.

358
00:19:10,191 --> 00:19:11,401
Just do yourself a favor.

359
00:19:11,610 --> 00:19:15,905
Okay? Go to school tomorrow, and mind your own business.

360
00:19:16,781 --> 00:19:17,781
All right?

361
00:19:19,618 --> 00:19:20,618
Dad.

362
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:24,289
Are you sad that you got fired?

363
00:19:27,250 --> 00:19:28,460
Mostly angry.

364
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:31,838
But yeah.

365
00:19:33,757 --> 00:19:35,216
Maybe a little sad.

366
00:19:43,141 --> 00:19:44,684
All right, let's say grace.

367
00:19:50,023 --> 00:19:53,234
Thank you, god, for this food we are about to receive.

368
00:20:02,285 --> 00:20:05,372
That was the first time I held my father's hand.

369
00:20:05,789 --> 00:20:08,458
Our bodies and bless the hands that prepared it.

370
00:20:09,084 --> 00:20:10,085
Amen.

371
00:20:10,293 --> 00:20:11,461
Amen. Amen.

372
00:20:14,255 --> 00:20:17,425
Hey, George Jr., wait your turn.

373
00:20:17,634 --> 00:20:23,807
I wouldn't touch my brother's hand until 17 years later, thanks to the invention of purell.

374
00:20:38,613 --> 00:20:40,031
You know what I find comforting?

375
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,240
What's that, baby?

376
00:20:41,574 --> 00:20:45,286
In a world filled with uncertainty, this place will be here forever.

377
00:20:47,539 --> 00:20:49,582
Hey, Sheldon, how you doing?
